From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:24:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wpt: Add a crashtest for terminating workers that create
 promises

Eight dedicated workers keep creating promises in platform code (a
ReadableStream's start promise and a reader's read promise) and are
terminated together. Before servo-quickjs Q36, QuickJS handled the
interrupt that termination requests inside NewPromiseObject, and the
worker panicked on the assert in Promise::new_in_realm. The test is
engine-neutral, waits without timers, and its workers stop by
themselves after 10 s if termination fails, so it could be upstreamed
to WPT.

Validation: `./mach test-wpt --profile checked-release --repeat 10` on the test, on ohos-main c5a6c8ef59d: CRASH 10/10 with QuickJS on servo-quickjs a5ebf1f, all at the promise.rs:259 assert; PASS 10/10 with 2de9592 (the previous patch) and with SpiderMonkey. `./mach test-tidy` passes the WPT lint and manifest checks; its only error, a cargo-deny advisory for ctutils 0.4.3, is on ohos-main too.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote the test from the fuzz finding and ran the checks above)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
